    "examples": [
      {
        "question_text": "Generate each number pattern for $x=0,1,2,3,4$.\n(a) $4x$\n(b) $2x+3$",
        "solution_text": "Substitute the **given** values in order.\n(a) $4(0)=0$\n$4(1)=4$\n$4(2)=8$\n$4(3)=12$\n$4(4)=16$\nThe pattern is $0,4,8,12,16$.\n(b) Multiply by $2$ before adding $3$.\n$2(0)+3=3$\n$2(1)+3=5$\n$2(2)+3=7$\n$2(3)+3=9$\n$2(4)+3=11$\nThe pattern is $3,5,7,9,11$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Generate each number pattern for $x=1,2,3,4$.\n(a) $3x-8$\n(b) $7-2x$",
        "solution_text": "(a) Multiply each input by $3$, then subtract $8$.\n$3(1)-8=-5$\n$3(2)-8=-2$\n$3(3)-8=1$\n$3(4)-8=4$\nThe pattern is $-5,-2,1,4$.\n(b) Keep the subtraction in the given order.\n$7-2(1)=5$\n$7-2(2)=3$\n$7-2(3)=1$\n$7-2(4)=-1$\nThe pattern is $5,3,1,-1$."
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Find the value directly, without listing earlier terms.\n(a) The pattern rule is $5x+1$. Find the value when $x=20$.\n(b) The pattern rule is $6-3x$. Find the value when $x=13$.",
        "solution_text": "Substitute the requested input straight into the rule.\n(a) $\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}5(20)+1\\\\&=100+1\\\\&=101\\end{aligned}$\n(b) $\\begin{aligned}&\\mathrel{\\phantom{=}}6-3(13)\\\\&=6-39\\\\&=-33\\end{aligned}$"
      },
      {
        "question_text": "Generate the number pattern from $-6x$ for $x=0,1,2,3,4$.",
        "solution_text": "Multiply each input by $-6$.\n$-6(0)=0$\n$-6(1)=-6$\n$-6(2)=-12$\n$-6(3)=-18$\n$-6(4)=-24$\nThe pattern is $0,-6,-12,-18,-24$."
      }
    ],
